      "name": "WTT - Fusion Hub",
      "slug": "wtt-fusion-hub",
      "teaser": "Want your front sight to have more picatinny rails? Now you can, thanks to the Fusion Hub!",
      "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/2809.png",
      "downloads": 2956,
      "favourites_count": 0,
      "description": "<p>Qwerty can do something other than port old and/or Oddba mods? Apparently so! With the help of the WTT Team, there’s now some spicy <em>new</em> bundles for you to add to your game!</p>\n<p>I’m happy to bring you the first thing I’ve made to the game, the Unity Fusion Hub - A picatinny front sight mount that allows you to have an above-bore attachment point as well as a front sight.</p>\n<p>Coming in Black and FDE with both folding and fixed irons, you can attach either a canted picatinny adapter, or two picatinny rails by foregoing the front sight. They can be purchased from Skier LL3,.</p>\n<p>Both 3.11 <em><strong>AND</strong></em> 3.10/3.9 downloads can be found at the link, make sure you grab the right one for your install!</p>\n<p>If anyone finds any bugs, lemme know in the comments and I can try to get them fixed - Since this is my first scratch-built I expect there might be one or two things I’ve forgotten.</p>\n<p>Credits to Tron, Groovey, Epic, and the rest of the team for helping me get these from blender all the way into the game.</p>\n",
